    "restrictions": "Permission \"Use MCP Server\" off by default, granted per workspace; the company administrator must enable MCP OAuth and approve the client's redirect URI; only allowlisted AI clients (Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, OpenAI Codex, Claude Code, VS Code); agent rights = dashboard rights, checked per request; does not work with IP Allowlisting; asterisked tools need the campaigns API beta program. Rate limits not documented.",
    "restricted_by": "Company administrator in Braze (OAuth, permissions, mass token revocation); Braze (client allowlist, beta program)",
    "governance_logic": "1) PII excluded by design (no user-level tools; only aggregates and configuration). 2) Dashboard rights inherited and checked per request; deactivated users lose access immediately. 3) Multi-level access: \"Use MCP Server\" permission (off by default) + OAuth enabled by admin + redirect URI approval + client allowlist. 4) Batch limits (catalogues <= 50 items) and pagination. 5) Campaign edits recorded under the user's name in the change history. 6) Nested agent: send_operator_prompt hands tasks to BrazeAI Operator in the background. 7) Beta gating (15 campaign tools, 3 segment tools). 8) No server-side confirmation: \"Braze receives and executes the tool call as the AI model sends it\".",
    "structure": "Standard",
    "structure_note": "Standard, but with a nested vendor agent (BrazeAI Operator); two regional endpoints (US mcp.braze.com, EU mcp.braze.eu), each works with any cluster",
    "actions_comment": "71 according to the documentation: 37 reading, 34 changing; 18 require the beta program",
    "tokens": "Cannot be determined",
    "token_method": "Exact descriptions and schemas not published; with 71 tools probably considerable",
    "agent_cannot": "User data (PII): profiles, export, deletion; Canvas is read-only; send messages directly (Messaging API); drag-and-drop templates; delete templates and content blocks; administration (users, rights, API keys, company settings); without beta: create/edit campaigns and segments.",
    "docs_recs": "Do not use auto-mode in the AI client; \"review any AI-proposed action before implementing it\"; \"Compare high-impact recommendations against source data\"; name the workspace explicitly in every request (production vs staging), otherwise the agent may \"choose an unexpected workspace\"; specify dates and metrics; ask the agent which tools it used.",
    "gov_promises": "\"non-PII Braze data\" / \"Tools that expose user-level PII are not available\"; \"An agent can never exceed your own access\"; campaign edits visible in the change history; \"Braze does not see your original natural-language prompt\"; disclaimer: Braze \"not liable for instructions generated by, or responses conveyed through, third-party MCP clients\"; privacy policy: Braze is processor for customer data, \"We maintain human oversight and do not make decisions based solely on automated processing\" (Braze's own AI); no overall MCP activity log described.",
